==English==

===Etymology===
1718, "untrustful, suspicious", either from {{suffix|leer|y|lang=en}}, or from dialectal {{m|en|lere}}, {{suffix|lear|t1=learning, knowledge|y|lang=en}}. More at {{l|en|leer}}, {{l|en|lear}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}
# [[cautious|Cautious]], [[hesitant]], or [[nervous]] about something; having [[reservations]] or [[concern]]s.
#: ''Since he was bitten by a dog when he was young, he has always been '''leery''' of animals.''

